# {{.Name}}

Generated with `go run github.com/Arif9878/common/go/cmd/newservice@{{.Version}}`. It is built on the [common library](https://github.com/Arif9878/common): read its README for what each piece does.

| File | |
|---|---|
| `main.go` | The fx application: configuration from the environment, observability, lifecycle, the admin server (`/live`, `/ready`, `/startup`, `/metrics`) and the Echo API server{{if .Postgres}}, PostgreSQL{{end}}. |
| `internal/api/` | The API. Handlers return errors; they become problem+json responses with the status of their kind.{{if .Postgres}} `migrations/` holds the goose migrations applied at startup.{{end}} |
| `main_test.go` | Starts the whole service and calls it.{{if .Postgres}} Needs `POSTGRES_TEST_URL`.{{end}} |
| `Dockerfile`, `k8s/deployment.yaml` | Build and deployment: identity from `OTEL_*`, probes on the admin port, a grace period longer than the shutdown timeout. |

## Run

```sh
go mod tidy
{{- if .Postgres}}
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost POSTGRES_DATABASE={{.Ident}} POSTGRES_USER=postgres POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres POSTGRES_SSLMODE=disable \
{{- end}}
LOG_FORMAT=text go run .
curl -s 'localhost:8080/v1/hello?name=Ada'
curl -s localhost:9090/ready
```

Configuration is environment variables only; the common library's ENVIRONMENT.md lists them.

## Test

```sh
{{if .Postgres}}POSTGRES_TEST_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/{{.Ident}} {{end}}go test -race ./...
```

## Upgrade the common library

Use one version for every `github.com/Arif9878/common/...` module:

```sh
go get github.com/Arif9878/common/go@vX.Y.Z github.com/Arif9878/common/go/fx@vX.Y.Z{{if .Postgres}} github.com/Arif9878/common/go/datastore/postgres@vX.Y.Z github.com/Arif9878/common/go/testkit/pgtest@vX.Y.Z{{end}}
go mod tidy
```

Read the release notes (CHANGELOG.md in the library) for breaking changes first.
